  "question": {
    "text": "A function $\\mathrm{f}$ from the set of natural numbers to integers defined by $\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{n})=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}\\frac{\\mathrm{n}-1}{2} \\text {, when } n \\text { isodd } \\\\ \\frac{\\mathrm{n}}{2} \\text {, when } \\mathrm{n} \\text { is even }\\end{array}\\right.$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2EIG6",
      "text": "\nneither one-one nor onto\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3WYuX",
      "text": "\none-one but not onto\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HfCGh",
      "text": "\nonto but not one-one\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "49XUq",
      "text": "\none-one and onto both.",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f: N \\rightarrow 1$\n$f(1)=0, f(2)=-1, f(3)=-1, f(4)=-2$\n$f(5)=2$, and $f(6)=-3$ so on.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/hAuAkB1tVJ7VkcIH2Z_ytAT4-Bh5p6GUix03MML7TIY.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nIn this type of function every element of set $\\mathrm{A}$ has unique image in set $\\mathrm{B}$ and there is no element left in set $\\mathrm{B}$. Hence $\\mathrm{f}$ is one-one and onto function.",
    "image": null
  },
